  EN.G.reported = lines(`
    He said, "I am tired."|He said that he was tired.|He said that he is tired.|He said that I was tired.|He said that he were tired.~Lùi thì: am → was; đổi ngôi: I → he.
    She said, "I like apples."|She said that she liked apples.|She said that she like apples.|She said that I liked apples.|She said that she liking apples.~Lùi thì: like → liked; I → she.
    Tom said, "I will help you."|Tom said that he would help me.|Tom said that he will help me.|Tom said that I would help me.|Tom said that he would helped me.~will → would; I → he; you → me.
    Lan said, "I can swim."|Lan said that she could swim.|Lan said that she can swim.|Lan said that I could swim.|Lan said that she could swam.~can → could; I → she.
    "Where do you live?" he asked me.|He asked me where I lived.|He asked me where did I live.|He asked me where do I live.|He asked me where I live.~Câu hỏi gián tiếp: không đảo ngữ, lùi thì: live → lived.
    "Are you hungry?" she asked me.|She asked me if I was hungry.|She asked me if was I hungry.|She asked me if I am hungry.|She asked me are you hungry.~Câu hỏi Yes/No gián tiếp: if/whether + S + V (lùi thì).
    "Don't be late," the teacher said to us.|The teacher told us not to be late.|The teacher told us don't be late.|The teacher told us to be not late.|The teacher said us not to be late.~Mệnh lệnh phủ định: told + O + not to + V.
    "Please close the door," she said to me.|She asked me to close the door.|She asked me close the door.|She asked me closing the door.|She said me to close the door.~Lời yêu cầu: asked + O + to + V.
    Mai said, "I am doing my homework now."|Mai said that she was doing her homework then.|Mai said that she is doing her homework now.|Mai said that she was doing my homework now.|Mai said that she did her homework then.~am doing → was doing; my → her; now → then.
    He said, "I bought a new bike yesterday."|He said that he had bought a new bike the day before.|He said that he has bought a new bike yesterday.|He said that he had bought a new bike tomorrow.|He said that I had bought a new bike the day before.~bought → had bought; yesterday → the day before.
  `);
